# Cursor Execution Engine - Logistics AI

## Role
Cursor is the primary technical execution engine for Logistics AI. Philippe provides product/structural approval; ChatGPT may provide execution prompts. Cursor should investigate, implement, test, commit, push, and handle DEV deploy/database work whenever credentials are already available.

## Before changing anything
1. Inspect current Git state, open PRs, recent commits, existing migrations, Supabase DEV, Vercel DEV, and existing domain modules before creating anything.
2. Reuse existing financial, DRE, service order, party/address, compliance, vehicle, driver, parking and car-wash concepts. Do not duplicate them.
3. Read all alwaysApply Cursor rules before work.
4. Keep Logistics-specific operational ownership in Logistics; shared identity/company/Party/entitlement foundations belong to PSCS One.
5. Work on a branch unless a repository-specific approved workflow says otherwise.

## Execution model
- Prefer a full autonomous execution pass instead of repeated manual command loops.
- Run safe discovery and validation without asking the user.
- Run available tests/build/lint and task-specific database checks.
- Commit/push and open/update PR when internally green.
- DEV is the first target.

## Local Windows mode
Canonical local root: D:\PSCS\Projetos\logistics-ai-erp
When running in Cursor Desktop, use integrated terminal/PowerShell from that path.
Do not ask Philippe to run commands manually when Cursor can run them.

## Cloud mode
Cursor Cloud cannot access the local D:\ drive or Windows PowerShell. Use the cloud checkout and configured remote integrations.

## Human intervention only when required
Ask Philippe only for:
- 2FA/login/OAuth consent
- missing secret/credential
- destructive or irreversible operation
- PROD deployment/promotion
- unresolved product/business decision

State one clear human action and continue all remaining safe work.

## Environment and production safety
- DEV first.
- PROD is protected and requires explicit Philippe approval for each promotion/deployment.
- Existing rules that imply automatic PROD publication are superseded by this rule.
- Never expose secrets or service-role values.
- Structural DB changes require versioned migration and DEV validation first.
- Do not silently edit migrations already applied.
